  "planning_notes": [
    "Arduino Uno pin ownership: all program-owned ports map to the explicit wiring in the prose and the previously recognized devices list; no rewiring or substitutions are performed.",
    "Green LED model defaults to true (HIGH) to satisfy 'no danger green constant on'; red LED model defaults to false (LOW) so it starts off.",
    "HC-SR04 distance conversion and hazard thresholds are handled in SysML; the ultrasonic catalog ports only provide distance (cm) and validity.",
    "TM1637 invalid_policy is set to 'blank' so SysML can request blanking for invalid/out-of-range danger level.",
    "Serial reporting format assumption: when the serial trigger becomes true, the system prints the single numeric value last_danger_duration_ms in ms (no fixed text prefix/suffix specified).",
    "D2 was omitted in the previous contract but is present in the authoritative device role inventory; it is represented as a program-owned digital_output on D2 with an explicit default model value false. The original prose does not specify D2 behavior, so the SysML logic must define its intended meaning."
  ],
